        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(goal-driver): completion contracts, wait barriers, and an optional completion judge",
        "body": "# feat(goal-driver): completion contracts, wait barriers, and an optional completion judge\r\n\r\n> **Stacked on #102261** (`feat/interactive-parity`) — only the last **3 commits** are new here\r\n> (`82879720c8`, `21792a1a3f`, `67c5600a13`). Merge the parity PR first; this one then reduces to\r\n> a small, purely-additive goal-driver series.\r\n\r\n## What\r\n\r\nThree opt-in upgrades to the experimental goal driver that make long goal runs **converge**\r\ninstead of firing continuations until the no-progress ceiling trips. \r\n\r\n### 1. Completion contracts (`82879720c8`)\r\n\r\n`SessionGoal` gains an optional structured contract — `outcome / verification / constraints[] /\r\nboundaries[] / stopWhen` — settable at goal-create time or later via the new **`set_goal_contract`**\r\ntool. The driver folds the contract block into **every continuation prompt**, so each nudge restates\r\nwhat \"done\" means and which constraints bound the work, instead of re-sending a bare objective.\r\n\r\n- Absent or all-empty contracts are dropped on normalize → a free-form goal's prompt is\r\n  **byte-for-byte unchanged**.\r\n- Also fixes a pre-existing broken `completeQueuedChatTurn(2-arg)` call in\r\n  `driver.integration-probe.test.ts` that left `tsgo:test` red on the base branch.\r\n\r\n### 2. Wait barriers — gate g5 (`21792a1a3f`)\r\n\r\nGoals can now **park** instead of burning continuation turns on async waits. `SessionGoal` gains an\r\noptional barrier (`waitingUntil` epoch **or** `waitingOnSessionKey`), surfaced via the new\r\n**`set_goal_wait`** tool (`seconds` backoff | `session_key` watch). New driver gate **g5**:\r\n\r\n- While a barrier is set and unsatisfied → re-arm at the floor, do **not** fire, and do **not**\r\n  consume a no-progress turn from the ceiling.\r\n- A satisfied barrier (deadline passed / watched session's run ended) clears itself; the next wake\r\n  resumes normal gating. Barriers auto-drop on any goal status change.\r\n\r\nThis is the \"waiting on CI / waiting on a subagent\" primitive: the goal stays alive without the\r\ndriver nudging a session that has nothing to do yet.\r\n\r\n### 3. Optional LLM completion judge (`67c5600a13`)\r\n\r\nConfig-gated via **`tools.experimental.goalDriver.judge.enabled` (default: off)**. After a goal turn\r\ncompletes and gates g1–g5 pass — and before a continuation fires — a bounded judge call classifies\r\nthe run: **`done`** → mark the goal complete (no continuation), **`wait`** → park behind the g5\r\nbarrier, **`continue`** → fire exactly as before.\r\n\r\n- **No new provider plumbing.** The judge reuses the existing simple-completion utility-model seam\r\n  (`prepareSimpleCompletionModelForAgent` + `completeWithPreparedSimpleCompletionModel`) — the same\r\n  seam `conversation-label-generator` uses. `judge.modelRef` overrides the model if desired.\r\n- **Fail-open by construction.** Unavailable model, transport error, empty/unparseable output, or a\r\n  thrown judge all resolve to a normal continuation — a broken judge can never wedge progress; the\r\n  no-progress ceiling remains the backstop.\r\n- **No async-gap races.** The judge await re-checks the pre-fire gates before firing\r\n  (queue-nonempty → re-arm; goal deactivated mid-judge → safe no-op), so a user message landing\r\n  during judge deliberation behaves exactly like the sync path.\r\n\r\n## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nToday the goal driver fires continuations blindly until the no-progress ceiling trips: a goal whose\r\nwork is actually finished keeps getting nudged, a goal waiting on CI or a subagent burns its\r\ncontinuation budget on \"still waiting\" turns, and each nudge re-sends a bare objective with no\r\ndefinition of done. With contracts + barriers + judge enabled, a goal run converges instead: every\r\ncontinuation restates the verification surface (contract) → async waits park instead of spinning\r\n(barrier) → the driver notices verifiable completion instead of nudging a finished session until the\r\nceiling trips (judge). Each piece is independently useful and independently off by default.\r\n\r\n## Behavior when you change nothing\r\n\r\nNone. No contract → identical prompts. No barrier → g5 passes trivially. No judge config → the\r\ndriver fires continuations exactly as on main. All config additions are `.strict()` zod objects with\r\nhelp + labels wired.\r\n\r\n## Example\r\n\r\n```jsonc\r\n// openclaw.jsonc\r\n{\r\n  \"tools\": {\r\n    \"experimental\": {\r\n      \"goalDriver\": {\r\n        \"enabled\": true,\r\n        \"judge\": { \"enabled\": true } // optional; uses the agent's utility model\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n```text\r\nagent → set_goal_contract { outcome: \"PR #42 merged\", verification: \"gh pr view 42 → MERGED\",\r\n                            stopWhen: \"CI green and merged\" }\r\nagent → set_goal_wait     { seconds: 300 }        // parked: waiting on CI\r\ndriver: [g5] barrier unsatisfied → re-arm (no ceiling turn consumed)\r\ndriver: barrier cleared → gates pass → judge → { verdict: \"done\", reason: \"PR is merged\" }\r\ndriver: goal marked complete — no further continuations\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- **40** passing in the focused goal-driver suite (`node scripts/test-projects.mjs\r\n  src/agents/goal-driver/`) plus **27** in `src/config/sessions/goals.test.ts`, including new\r\n  suites: contract prompt folding, g5 barrier gating (fire/park/clear/auto-drop), judge branching\r\n  (done/continue/wait), judge fail-open (undefined/throw), mid-judge race regressions\r\n  (queue-flip / run-flip / goal-deactivated), and the atomic `requireActiveStatus` store guard.\r\n  The race regressions were proven fail-without/pass-with: the pre-fix judge path fired/mutated\r\n  unconditionally after the await.\r\n- `pnpm tsgo:prod` and `pnpm tsgo:test` clean (test-side was red on the base branch before commit 1;\r\n  commit 1 fixes the broken `completeQueuedChatTurn` call in `driver.integration-probe.test.ts`).\r\n",
        "branch": "feat/goal-driver-hermes-upgrades",
